Package: cldreducer
Title: Reduce Compact Letter Displays
Version: 0.3.0
Authors@R:
  c(
    person("John", "Ennis", , "john.m.ennis@aigora.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Aigora", role = c("cph", "fnd"))
  )
Description: Reduces compact letter displays (CLDs) of all pairwise
    comparisons. A CLD gives two groups a common letter exactly when they are
    not significantly different. The package finds a display with the fewest
    letter assignments or distinct letters that keeps every relationship.
    The optional CLD-sigma objective is the assignment-minimum clique covering
    problem of Ennis, Fayle, and Ennis
    (2012) <doi:10.1145/2133803.2275596>, solved as a mixed-integer linear
    program with 'HiGHS'. The default CLD-C method selects full maximal
    cliques with the fewest letters. Among displays with the selected minimum objective, it returns
    one fixed canonical display, so the result does not depend on the
    solver. The package includes the wheat yield example of Piepho (2004)
    <doi:10.1198/1061860043515>.
